## 6. Gotchas

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fusermount3: mount failed: Operation not permitted` | `fuse-overlayfs` run directly, no caps | wrap in `unshare -Urm` |
| `unshare: unshare failed: Operation not permitted` | RuntimeDefault (or profile missing `unshare`) | Localhost profile from section 3 |
| terminal / VS Code shows empty `/home/coder/workspace` | mount done by agent `startup_script` or a terminal | mount in the container entrypoint, start the agent inside |
| `kubectl exec`: `error executing setns process` | entrypoint did `exec unshare` (PID 1 moved) | background the `unshare` tree, `wait` |
| `kubectl exec` shows empty workspace | expected, original namespace | debug with `nsenter` (below) |
| `wrong final value type: attribute "spec": attribute "volumes": tuple required` | bare Pod in `kubernetes_manifest`; API server adds the SA token volume | use a Deployment |
| `cannot list resource "customresourcedefinitions"` at plan | `kubernetes_manifest` schema discovery | CRD `get`/`list` ClusterRole |
| template fix not picked up | `coder start` keeps the workspace's template version | `coder update <ws>` |
| `Transport endpoint is not connected` | `fuse-overlayfs` process died | restart the workspace (entrypoint remounts) |
| editing/deleting base files: `Permission denied` / `Value too large for defined data type`; files show as `nobody` | lower owned by a uid not mapped in the nested namespace (reconciler writes as root) | `fuse-overlayfs -o ...,squash_to_root` |
| `failed to set MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP ... invalid argument` at container start | hostPath/PV on a filesystem without idmapped-mount support (`hostUsers: false`) | put the tree on ext4/XFS |
| `umount: ... must be superuser to unmount` from a terminal | the terminal is in the inner namespace | rebase through `ws-base` (controller in the outer namespace) |
| `pinned base ... is not materialized on this node` | base commit GC'd, or pod moved to a node without it | materialize pinned commits; exempt them from GC |

---

## 7. Verify and debug

From a Coder terminal or `coder ssh`:

```sh
id                                              # uid=1000(coder)
grep ' /home/coder/workspace ' /proc/self/mountinfo   # fuse-overlayfs
ls -la /home/coder/workspace
```

Where edits land (from `kubectl exec`, original namespace):

```sh
kubectl exec deploy/<workspace> -- ls -la /data/overlay/upper /data/lower
# edits in upper; deletions as c--------- whiteouts; lower unchanged
```

See the overlay from `kubectl exec` (profile must allow `setns`):

```sh
kubectl exec -it deploy/<workspace> -- sh -c 'nsenter -t $(pgrep -x fuse-overlayfs) -U -m --preserve-credentials sh'
```

You appear as root there (uid 1000 on disk). Joining the agent's inner user namespace directly fails for the mount namespace (`reassociate to namespace 'ns/mnt' failed`) because the mount namespace belongs to the outer nested user namespace.

